1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,553
Seven in the morning. The build is red, and the message says 401.

2
00:00:05,103 --> 00:00:06,303
Ten minutes later,

3
00:00:06,303 --> 00:00:07,969
a different build is red,

4
00:00:07,969 --> 00:00:09,635
and the message says 403.

5
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:11,768
Then a third one says not found.

6
00:00:11,768 --> 00:00:14,767
Then a fourth says the repository is offline.

7
00:00:15,317 --> 00:00:16,182
Four failures.

8
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,601
Four different numbers.

9
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:19,515
Most people read the last line,

10
00:00:19,515 --> 00:00:20,626
see build failure,

11
00:00:20,626 --> 00:00:22,848
and start changing things at random.

12
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:25,952
Today we learn to read the first error.

13
00:00:25,952 --> 00:00:28,834
We break our own Nexus Repository four ways,

14
00:00:28,834 --> 00:00:29,555
on purpose,

15
00:00:29,555 --> 00:00:30,865
and we fix each one.

16
00:00:31,415 --> 00:00:35,250
Then we prove the whole domain with a script that checks seven things.

17
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:35,743
Break it,

18
00:00:35,743 --> 00:00:36,127
fix it,

19
00:00:36,127 --> 00:00:36,620
prove it.

20
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,599
Here is what to expect.

21
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:42,389
One: the Nexus domain, on one page.

22
00:00:42,939 --> 00:00:45,222
Two: the scenario, and the seven checks.

23
00:00:45,772 --> 00:00:46,978
Three: a live demo,

24
00:00:46,978 --> 00:00:50,089
in the real Nexus screens and in a real terminal.

25
00:00:50,089 --> 00:00:50,978
Four failures,

26
00:00:50,978 --> 00:00:51,804
one fix each,

27
00:00:51,804 --> 00:00:52,756
then the proof,

28
00:00:52,756 --> 00:00:53,772
and the cleanup.

29
00:00:54,322 --> 00:00:57,607
Four: what to do when a check fails, and where to find the lab.

30
00:00:58,157 --> 00:01:00,952
This is the mastery lesson of the Nexus domain.

31
00:01:02,502 --> 00:01:06,577
The Nexus domain, on one page. Eight objectives, four lessons.

32
00:01:07,127 --> 00:01:09,322
Lesson 173: hosted,

33
00:01:09,322 --> 00:01:11,252
proxy and group repositories,

34
00:01:11,252 --> 00:01:13,847
and how to install Nexus and secure it.

35
00:01:14,397 --> 00:01:18,702
Lesson 174: snapshot and release repositories,

36
00:01:18,702 --> 00:01:20,599
publishing and retrieving,

37
00:01:20,599 --> 00:01:23,079
and settings.xml with credentials.

38
00:01:23,629 --> 00:01:26,038
Lesson 175: immutability,

39
00:01:26,038 --> 00:01:27,622
retention and provenance,

40
00:01:27,622 --> 00:01:28,700
then permissions,

41
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,157
backups and monitoring.

42
00:01:30,707 --> 00:01:32,081
Today: troubleshooting,

43
00:01:32,081 --> 00:01:33,694
by reading the first error.

44
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:36,681
And one scenario that uses the heart of all eight.

45
00:01:38,231 --> 00:01:39,080
The scenario.

46
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:42,673
An artifact pipeline for Cloud Cart that you can prove.

47
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:43,522
Seven checks,

48
00:01:43,522 --> 00:01:44,567
run by a script.

49
00:01:45,117 --> 00:01:46,321
One: Nexus is up.

50
00:01:46,321 --> 00:01:49,084
Two: the releases repository is online,

51
00:01:49,084 --> 00:01:52,626
and it will not accept a second copy of a release.

52
00:01:53,176 --> 00:01:55,949
Three: the deployer can publish a snapshot.

53
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:58,979
Four: the deployer cannot delete from releases.

54
00:01:59,529 --> 00:02:05,076
Five: the release jar matches its checksum. Six: the cleanup and backup tasks exist.

55
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:07,454
Seven: no password in the code.

56
00:02:07,454 --> 00:02:08,869
That last one is a trap,

57
00:02:08,869 --> 00:02:10,874
and we will fall in it on purpose.

58
00:02:11,424 --> 00:02:15,562
The script checks the facts, not your word. That is what makes it independent.

59
00:02:16,112 --> 00:02:17,968
Seven of seven, is mastery.

60
00:02:19,518 --> 00:02:21,035
Real Nexus Repository,

61
00:02:21,035 --> 00:02:22,896
signed in as administrator.

62
00:02:22,896 --> 00:02:27,377
Everything from the last three lessons is here: the repositories,

63
00:02:27,377 --> 00:02:28,273
the deployer,

64
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:28,894
the role,

65
00:02:28,894 --> 00:02:29,859
and the tasks.

66
00:02:29,859 --> 00:02:31,858
Today we break it on purpose,

67
00:02:31,858 --> 00:02:32,548
four ways,

68
00:02:32,548 --> 00:02:33,513
and we fix it.

69
00:02:34,063 --> 00:02:35,770
One habit solves most of it.

70
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:37,051
Read the first error,

71
00:02:37,051 --> 00:02:38,088
not the last one.

72
00:02:38,088 --> 00:02:40,101
The last line says build failure,

73
00:02:40,101 --> 00:02:41,748
and that tells you nothing.

74
00:02:41,748 --> 00:02:43,577
The first error tells you why.

75
00:02:44,127 --> 00:02:44,507
First,

76
00:02:44,507 --> 00:02:45,329
the terminal.

77
00:02:45,329 --> 00:02:47,163
The lab command is installed.

78
00:02:47,163 --> 00:02:49,124
Lab up checks that Nexus is up,

79
00:02:49,124 --> 00:02:51,338
and says where the results will go.

80
00:02:51,888 --> 00:02:52,827
Now lab check.

81
00:02:52,827 --> 00:02:55,309
It runs seven checks on our pipeline.

82
00:02:55,309 --> 00:02:55,912
Six pass.

83
00:02:55,912 --> 00:02:58,193
One fails: a password in the code.

84
00:02:58,193 --> 00:02:59,803
We will come back to it.

85
00:03:00,353 --> 00:03:01,119
Failure one.

86
00:03:01,119 --> 00:03:03,097
A deploy with a wrong password.

87
00:03:03,097 --> 00:03:04,374
We run Maven deploy,

88
00:03:04,374 --> 00:03:06,288
and for this one command only,

89
00:03:06,288 --> 00:03:08,075
we give it a wrong password.

90
00:03:14,825 --> 00:03:16,582
Now read the first error.

91
00:03:16,582 --> 00:03:17,706
Status code 401,

92
00:03:17,706 --> 00:03:18,619
Unauthorized.

93
00:03:18,619 --> 00:03:21,289
That means: I do not know who you are.

94
00:03:21,839 --> 00:03:24,226
Nexus never looked at any permission,

95
00:03:24,226 --> 00:03:26,160
because it never got that far.

96
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,902
So the fix is the password.

97
00:03:27,902 --> 00:03:28,740
Not the role,

98
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,223
and not the repository.

99
00:03:30,773 --> 00:03:36,256
We run the same command again, with the right password. Build success. One cause, one fix.

100
00:03:42,706 --> 00:03:43,510
Failure two.

101
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:45,855
A teammate trims the deployer role,

102
00:03:45,855 --> 00:03:47,998
and removes one privilege: edit,

103
00:03:47,998 --> 00:03:49,874
on the snapshots repository.

104
00:03:50,424 --> 00:03:51,533
We open Roles.

105
00:03:58,283 --> 00:03:59,819
We open cart deployer.

106
00:04:04,069 --> 00:04:05,627
And click Edit privileges.

107
00:04:08,877 --> 00:04:11,415
We filter by the snapshots repository.

108
00:04:15,065 --> 00:04:16,196
And untick edit.

109
00:04:17,946 --> 00:04:19,034
Then we confirm.

110
00:04:22,784 --> 00:04:23,872
And save the role.

111
00:04:28,622 --> 00:04:29,987
Now the deploy again.

112
00:04:41,437 --> 00:04:42,595
Status code 403,

113
00:04:42,595 --> 00:04:43,319
Forbidden.

114
00:04:43,319 --> 00:04:45,562
That means: I know who you are,

115
00:04:45,562 --> 00:04:47,298
and you are not allowed.

116
00:04:47,298 --> 00:04:49,179
It is not the same as 401.

117
00:04:49,179 --> 00:04:50,916
Nexus knew the deployer,

118
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:51,784
and said no.

119
00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:54,030
Why does Maven need edit?

120
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:55,727
After it uploads the jar,

121
00:04:55,727 --> 00:04:57,966
it updates a small metadata file,

122
00:04:57,966 --> 00:05:00,544
and updating a file counts as an edit.

123
00:05:00,544 --> 00:05:01,901
The fix is the role,

124
00:05:01,901 --> 00:05:02,851
so we go back.

125
00:05:03,401 --> 00:05:04,511
We open Roles.

126
00:05:11,261 --> 00:05:12,541
Then cart deployer.

127
00:05:17,091 --> 00:05:18,520
And Edit privileges.

128
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,001
We filter again.

129
00:05:28,051 --> 00:05:29,181
And we tick edit.

130
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:31,770
We confirm.

131
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:36,857
And we save the role.

132
00:05:41,407 --> 00:05:45,119
And we deploy once more. Build success. Failure two, fixed.

133
00:05:54,169 --> 00:05:55,265
Failure three.

134
00:05:55,265 --> 00:05:57,613
A pipeline asks for cart-core,

135
00:05:57,613 --> 00:05:58,709
version 1.0.1,

136
00:05:58,709 --> 00:06:00,979
from the releases repository.

137
00:06:00,979 --> 00:06:03,327
We ask Nexus for the pom file,

138
00:06:03,327 --> 00:06:05,988
and we print only the status code.

139
00:06:06,538 --> 00:06:06,806
404,

140
00:06:06,806 --> 00:06:07,476
not found.

141
00:06:07,476 --> 00:06:09,554
That is not a password problem,

142
00:06:09,554 --> 00:06:11,497
and not a permission problem.

143
00:06:11,497 --> 00:06:12,972
The file is not there,

144
00:06:12,972 --> 00:06:14,044
at that address.

145
00:06:14,044 --> 00:06:15,920
Either the address is wrong,

146
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,730
or the file does not exist.

147
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:18,802
We do not guess.

148
00:06:18,802 --> 00:06:19,338
We look.

149
00:06:19,888 --> 00:06:23,579
In the browser, we open Browse, and the releases repository.

150
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:28,846
First com.

151
00:06:32,096 --> 00:06:33,227
Then cloudcart.

152
00:06:36,177 --> 00:06:37,265
Then cart-core.

153
00:06:40,315 --> 00:06:42,348
Only one version exists,

154
00:06:42,348 --> 00:06:42,857
1.0.0.

155
00:06:42,857 --> 00:06:44,382
There is no 1.0.1.

156
00:06:44,382 --> 00:06:49,296
The pipeline asked for a release that was never published.

157
00:06:49,846 --> 00:06:51,623
So we fix the request,

158
00:06:51,623 --> 00:06:52,835
not the server.

159
00:06:52,835 --> 00:06:54,855
Version 1.0.0 does exist,

160
00:06:54,855 --> 00:06:57,441
and this time the answer is 200.

161
00:06:57,991 --> 00:07:01,406
One more cousin of this failure: stale metadata.

162
00:07:01,406 --> 00:07:05,391
Maven finds the newest snapshot by reading a small file,

163
00:07:05,391 --> 00:07:06,743
maven-metadata.xml.

164
00:07:06,743 --> 00:07:07,525
We read it,

165
00:07:07,525 --> 00:07:09,660
and it names the latest build.

166
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:11,703
Open System, Tasks.

167
00:07:17,953 --> 00:07:19,041
And Create task.

168
00:07:22,791 --> 00:07:26,577
It is in the Repair group: Rebuild Maven repository metadata.

169
00:07:26,577 --> 00:07:28,066
We do not need it today.

170
00:07:28,066 --> 00:07:30,301
We only need to know where it lives.

171
00:07:30,851 --> 00:07:31,648
Failure four.

172
00:07:31,648 --> 00:07:34,897
Someone takes the repository offline for maintenance,

173
00:07:34,897 --> 00:07:36,675
and forgets to bring it back.

174
00:07:37,225 --> 00:07:40,894
We open the repository list, and the releases repository.

175
00:07:44,844 --> 00:07:46,252
We click Take Offline.

176
00:07:49,602 --> 00:07:50,669
And we confirm.

177
00:07:54,919 --> 00:07:58,716
The page now says offline, and the button changes to Bring Online.

178
00:07:59,266 --> 00:08:00,310
Now the terminal.

179
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:02,091
We ask for the same pom file,

180
00:08:02,091 --> 00:08:03,873
and we print the status code,

181
00:08:03,873 --> 00:08:04,855
and the message.

182
00:08:05,405 --> 00:08:05,724
503,

183
00:08:05,724 --> 00:08:07,239
repository offline.

184
00:08:07,239 --> 00:08:09,630
A 503 says the server is fine,

185
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:12,740
but this one repository is not serving.

186
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,493
The password is right,

187
00:08:14,493 --> 00:08:15,928
the role is right,

188
00:08:15,928 --> 00:08:17,204
the file exists.

189
00:08:17,204 --> 00:08:19,037
Only the switch is off.

190
00:08:19,587 --> 00:08:20,974
We click Bring Online.

191
00:08:25,724 --> 00:08:26,791
And we confirm.

192
00:08:31,041 --> 00:08:35,947
And we ask again. 200. Four failures, read from the first error, and fixed.

193
00:08:36,497 --> 00:08:37,410
Now the proof.

194
00:08:37,410 --> 00:08:38,062
Lab check,

195
00:08:38,062 --> 00:08:38,453
again.

196
00:08:38,453 --> 00:08:39,822
Everything works now,

197
00:08:39,822 --> 00:08:42,364
except the trap: one check still fails.

198
00:08:42,914 --> 00:08:47,107
Leak check looks for passwords in the files of this folder.

199
00:08:47,107 --> 00:08:49,523
And it finds one: settings-ci.xml,

200
00:08:49,523 --> 00:08:51,655
with a password in plain text.

201
00:08:51,655 --> 00:08:52,508
An old file,

202
00:08:52,508 --> 00:08:54,285
forgotten in the project.

203
00:08:54,835 --> 00:08:56,120
We treat it as real,

204
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,147
so it is leaked.

205
00:08:57,147 --> 00:08:57,918
Two actions.

206
00:08:57,918 --> 00:08:58,304
First,

207
00:08:58,304 --> 00:09:00,424
remove the file from the project.

208
00:09:00,974 --> 00:09:04,643
Second, change that password in Nexus, in Security, Users.

209
00:09:09,293 --> 00:09:11,231
Removing the file is not enough,

210
00:09:11,231 --> 00:09:13,351
because copies and history keep it.

211
00:09:13,351 --> 00:09:14,925
The old password must die.

212
00:09:15,475 --> 00:09:19,422
Lab check one more time. Seven of seven. Every check passes.

213
00:09:19,972 --> 00:09:21,950
Results are part of the mastery.

214
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:23,928
The script saved them in a file.

215
00:09:23,928 --> 00:09:24,484
Print it.

216
00:09:24,484 --> 00:09:26,400
This is your evidence: keep it,

217
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,204
and share it.

218
00:09:27,754 --> 00:09:28,093
Last,

219
00:09:28,093 --> 00:09:28,905
the cleanup.

220
00:09:28,905 --> 00:09:31,546
Lab down keeps a copy of your evidence,

221
00:09:31,546 --> 00:09:34,188
and removes the test file it published.

222
00:09:34,188 --> 00:09:34,594
Nexus,

223
00:09:34,594 --> 00:09:35,813
your repositories,

224
00:09:35,813 --> 00:09:37,845
your role and your tasks stay.

225
00:09:38,395 --> 00:09:40,743
Ask Nexus for the test component.

226
00:09:40,743 --> 00:09:41,312
Nothing.

227
00:09:41,312 --> 00:09:43,163
The scenario left no mess.

228
00:09:43,163 --> 00:09:43,661
Broken,

229
00:09:43,661 --> 00:09:44,088
fixed,

230
00:09:44,088 --> 00:09:44,586
proved,

231
00:09:44,586 --> 00:09:45,511
written down,

232
00:09:45,511 --> 00:09:46,579
and cleaned up.

233
00:09:46,579 --> 00:09:47,717
That is mastery.

234
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:51,827
When a check fails, the number tells you where to look.

235
00:09:52,377 --> 00:09:55,577
401: the password is wrong. Fix the credential.

236
00:09:56,127 --> 00:10:01,738
403: the role is too small. Fix the privilege, and read which action was refused.

237
00:10:02,288 --> 00:10:07,642
404: the address is wrong, or the file was never published. Open Browse, and look.

238
00:10:08,192 --> 00:10:11,947
503: the repository is offline. Bring it online.

239
00:10:12,497 --> 00:10:15,462
And a password in the code: remove it, and change it.

240
00:10:17,012 --> 00:10:19,807
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

241
00:10:20,357 --> 00:10:28,591
One: the repository, github.com/it-waves/devops-ai, in the folder academy/lab.

242
00:10:29,141 --> 00:10:35,520
Two: the files, lab176.sh and shortcuts176.sh.

243
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:41,723
Three: load the short names with source shortcuts176.sh. Then lab up.

244
00:10:42,273 --> 00:10:48,140
Four: lab check runs the seven checks. Lab down cleans up. Leak check looks for passwords.

245
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:53,015
Five: you need the Nexus and the project from the earlier lessons.

246
00:10:53,015 --> 00:10:55,374
Set your admin login in NEXUS_ADMIN,

247
00:10:55,374 --> 00:10:58,717
and your deployer in NEXUS_USER and NEXUS_PASSWORD.

248
00:10:59,267 --> 00:11:00,909
The link is in the description.

249
00:11:02,459 --> 00:11:04,230
Your turn, on your own machine.

250
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:07,745
One: lab up, then lab check. See which checks pass.

251
00:11:08,295 --> 00:11:12,178
Two: break your deploy with a wrong password, and read the 401.

252
00:11:12,728 --> 00:11:17,016
Three: take edit from the deployer, and read the 403. Then give it back.

253
00:11:17,566 --> 00:11:20,283
Four: ask for a version that does not exist,

254
00:11:20,283 --> 00:11:23,432
then take the repository offline and bring it back.

255
00:11:23,982 --> 00:11:26,019
Five: find the leaked password,

256
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:26,676
remove it,

257
00:11:26,676 --> 00:11:27,596
and change it.

258
00:11:27,596 --> 00:11:28,581
Then lab check,

259
00:11:28,581 --> 00:11:30,487
until you see seven of seven.

260
00:11:30,487 --> 00:11:31,406
Then lab down.

261
00:11:31,956 --> 00:11:33,684
Pause the video, and do it now.

262
00:11:49,234 --> 00:11:50,109
Quick check.

263
00:11:50,659 --> 00:11:54,157
A build says 401. Do you change the role, or the password?

264
00:11:54,707 --> 00:11:57,609
What is the difference between 401 and 403?

265
00:11:58,159 --> 00:12:02,532
A pipeline asks for a version, and gets 404. What do you do first?

266
00:12:03,082 --> 00:12:07,199
What does 503 tell you about the server, and about the repository?

267
00:12:07,749 --> 00:12:12,507
Objective covered: Nexus Repository mastery. The whole domain, proved.

268
00:12:13,057 --> 00:12:15,126
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

269
00:12:25,676 --> 00:12:29,815
Next: a new domain. GitHub Actions, where your code builds itself.

270
00:12:30,365 --> 00:12:33,693
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
